  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0147, and it contains six tables. The first table, Class, has four columns: Class_ID, Class_Name, Department_Name, and Grade. The Class_ID column is the primary key, and the other columns are all strings. The second table, Member, has eight columns: Age, Class_ID, Contact_Number, Email, Member_ID, Name, Password, and Workplace. The Member_ID column is the primary key, and the other columns are all strings. The third table, Announcement, has four columns: Announcement_Content, Announcement_ID, Announcement_Time, and Class_ID. The Announcement_ID column is the primary key, and the other columns are all strings. The fourth table, Message, has six columns: Message_Content, Read_Flag, Receiver_ID, Send_Time, Sender_ID, and a composite primary key consisting of Sender_ID, Receiver_ID, and Send_Time. The fifth table, Log, has five columns: Log_Content, Log_ID, Member_ID, Mood, and Time. The Log_ID column is the primary key, and the other columns are all strings. The sixth table, Application, has five columns: Application_Content, Application_ID, Application_Time, Approval_Flag, and Member_ID. The Application_ID column is the primary key, and the other columns are all strings. The tables are linked by foreign keys, with the Member table referencing the Class table, the Announcement table referencing the Class table, the Message table referencing the Member table, the Log table referencing the Member table, and the Application table referencing the Member table.",
  "gold_question": "The key features of the system are as follows:\n1.Class Management: Manage class information, including class name, department name, grade, etc.\n2.Member Management: Manage the information of class members, including member ID, name, password, email, age, workplace, contact number, etc.\n3.Announcement Management: Publish and manage class announcements, including announcement ID, announcement time, and announcement content.\n4.Message Management: Manage class messages, allowing members to send messages. The system records sender ID, receiver ID, message content, send time, and read status.\n5.Log Management: Record class logs, including log ID, log content, time, mood, etc. Each member can post their own logs.\n6.Leave Management: Manage class messages, including message ID, message time, message content, and message count. Each member can leave messages.\n7.Application Management: Handle applications submitted by class members, including application ID, application time, approval status, and application content.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0147.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0147\nCREATE TABLE `class` (\n  `class_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `class_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `department_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `grade` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`class_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `member` (\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `age` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_number` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `workplace` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `class_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`member_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `member_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`class_id`) REFERENCES `class` (`class_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `announcement` (\n  `announcement_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `announcement_content` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `announcement_time` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `class_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`announcement_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `announcement_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`class_id`) REFERENCES `class` (`class_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `message` (\n  `sender_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `receiver_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `send_time` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `message_content` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `read_flag` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sender_id`, `receiver_id`, `send_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `message_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`sender_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`member_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `message_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`receiver_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`member_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `log` (\n  `log_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `log_content` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `mood` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `time` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `member_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`log_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `log_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`member_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`member_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `application` (\n  `application_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `application_content` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `application_time` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `approval_flag` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `member_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`application_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `application_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`member_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`member_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
